      ram: {
        'Getting Started': {
          sections: [
            {
              title: 'Installation',
              content: `RAM (Resilient Adaptive Manager) provides PostgreSQL clustering with automatic failover and Raft consensus.

**Prerequisites:**
- PostgreSQL 12+ (tested up to PostgreSQL 17)
- Go 1.21+ (for building from source)
- C compiler (GCC 7.0+ or Clang 6.0+)
- PostgreSQL development headers
- OpenSSL 1.1.1+ (for TLS support)

**Build and Install:**
\`\`\`bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/pgElephant/ram.git
cd ram

# Build all components
make

# Install system-wide
sudo make install

# Verify installation
which ramd
which ramctrl
\`\`\`

**Install pgraft Extension:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Connect to PostgreSQL
\\c postgres

-- Create the extension
CREATE EXTENSION pgraft;

-- Verify installation
SELECT pgraft_version();
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'Components',
              content: `RAM consists of three main components that work together to provide enterprise-grade PostgreSQL clustering:

**1. pgraft (PostgreSQL Extension)**
- Implements Raft consensus algorithm inside PostgreSQL
- Provides automatic leader election and log replication
- Ensures 100% split-brain protection
- Runs as PostgreSQL background worker

**2. ramd (Cluster Management Daemon)**
- Monitors PostgreSQL instances and cluster health
- Coordinates failover operations
- Provides REST API for cluster management
- Exposes Prometheus metrics for monitoring

**3. ramctrl (Command-Line Control Utility)**
- Command-line interface for cluster management
- Supports cluster operations and configuration
- Provides administrative functions
- Enables scripting and automation

**Architecture Overview:**
\`\`\`
┌─────────────────┐    ┌─────────────────┐    ┌─────────────────┐
│   PostgreSQL    │    │   PostgreSQL    │    │   PostgreSQL    │
│   + pgraft      │    │   + pgraft      │    │   + pgraft      │
│   (Leader)      │◄──►│   (Follower)    │◄──►│   (Follower)    │
└─────────────────┘    └─────────────────┘    └─────────────────┘
         ▲                       ▲                       ▲
         │                       │                       │
         ▼                       ▼                       ▼
┌─────────────────┐    ┌─────────────────┐    ┌─────────────────┐
│      ramd       │    │      ramd       │    │      ramd       │
│  (Monitoring)   │    │  (Monitoring)   │    │  (Monitoring)   │
└─────────────────┘    └─────────────────┘    └─────────────────┘
         ▲                       ▲                       ▲
         └───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┘
                                 ▼
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │    ramctrl      │
                    │ (Administration)│
                    └─────────────────┘
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'Quick Start',
              content: `**Setting up a 3-node RAM cluster:**

**1. Prepare all nodes:**
\`\`\`bash
# On each node, install PostgreSQL and RAM components
# Configure PostgreSQL for replication
\`\`\`

**2. Configure PostgreSQL:**
\`\`\`conf
# postgresql.conf
shared_preload_libraries = 'pgraft'
wal_level = replica
max_wal_senders = 10
max_replication_slots = 10
hot_standby = on
\`\`\`

**3. Initialize the cluster:**
\`\`\`sql
-- On node1 (will become leader)
CREATE EXTENSION pgraft;
SELECT pgraft_init();

-- Check if leader
SELECT pgraft_is_leader();
\`\`\`

**4. Add nodes to cluster:**
\`\`\`sql
-- From the leader node
SELECT pgraft_add_node(2, '192.168.1.102', 7002);
SELECT pgraft_add_node(3, '192.168.1.103', 7003);

-- Verify cluster status
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_cluster_status();
\`\`\`

**5. Start ramd on all nodes:**
\`\`\`bash
# Start cluster management daemon
ramd --config /etc/ram/ramd.conf --daemon

# Check status
ramctrl status
\`\`\`

**6. Verify cluster health:**
\`\`\`bash
# Check cluster status
ramctrl status

# View cluster information
ramctrl info

# Check node health
ramctrl health
\`\`\``
            }
          ]
        },
        'pgraft Documentation': {
          sections: [
            {
              title: 'Overview',
              content: `**pgraft** is a PostgreSQL extension that implements the Raft consensus algorithm for distributed PostgreSQL clusters. It provides automatic leader election, log replication, and 100% split-brain protection.

**Key Features:**
- **Raft Consensus**: Based on etcd-io/raft implementation
- **Leader Election**: Automatic with quorum-based voting
- **Log Replication**: Consistent state across all nodes
- **Split-Brain Protection**: 100% guaranteed via Raft quorum
- **Leader-Only Node Addition**: Configuration changes only on leader, automatically replicated
- **Worker-Driven Architecture**: PostgreSQL background worker actively drives Raft ticks
- **Persistent Storage**: HardState, log entries, and snapshots survive crashes

**Production Ready:**
- 0 compilation errors/warnings
- PostgreSQL C coding standards compliant
- Persistent storage survives crashes
- Worker-driven architecture`
            },
            {
              title: 'Quick Example',
              content: `\`\`\`sql
-- Create extension
CREATE EXTENSION pgraft;

-- Initialize node
SELECT pgraft_init();

-- Check if current node is leader
SELECT pgraft_is_leader();

-- If leader, add other nodes
SELECT pgraft_add_node(2, '127.0.0.1', 7002);
SELECT pgraft_add_node(3, '127.0.0.1', 7003);

-- Get cluster status
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_cluster_status();
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'Architecture at a Glance',
              content: `\`\`\`
PostgreSQL Background Worker (C)
    ↓ Every 100ms
pgraft_go_tick() [C→Go]
    ↓
raftNode.Tick() [etcd-io/raft]
    ↓
Ready() messages
    ↓
raftProcessingLoop() [Goroutine]
    ↓
Persist → Send → Apply → Advance
\`\`\`

**Why pgraft?**

**Split-Brain Protection:**
pgraft provides **100% split-brain protection** through:
- **Quorum Requirement**: Leader needs majority votes (N/2 + 1)
- **Term Monotonicity**: Higher term always wins
- **Log Completeness**: Only up-to-date nodes can be elected
- **Single Leader Per Term**: Mathematical guarantee from Raft algorithm

**Automatic Replication:**
When you add a node to the leader, it **automatically appears on ALL other nodes**. You only need to run **ONE command on the leader**. The Raft consensus protocol handles everything else.

**Performance:**
- **Tick Interval**: 100ms (worker-driven)
- **Election Timeout**: 1000ms (default, configurable)
- **Heartbeat**: 100ms (default, configurable)
- **Memory**: ~50MB per node
- **CPU**: <1% idle, <5% during elections`
            },
            {
              title: 'Installation',
              content: `**Prerequisites:**
- PostgreSQL 17+ (recommended)
- Go 1.21+ (for building from source)
- Standard build tools (gcc, make)
- Root/sudo access for installation

**Building from Source:**
\`\`\`bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/pgElephant/pgraft.git
cd pgraft

# Build the extension
make

# Install the extension
sudo make install

# Verify installation
ls -la $(pg_config --pkglibdir)/pgraft.so
\`\`\`

**Database Setup:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Connect to your PostgreSQL database
\\c mydatabase

-- Create the extension
CREATE EXTENSION pgraft;

-- Verify installation
SELECT pgraft_version();
\`\`\`

**Quick Start:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Initialize the node
SELECT pgraft_init();

-- Check if current node is leader
SELECT pgraft_is_leader();

-- If leader, add other nodes
SELECT pgraft_add_node(2, '127.0.0.1', 7002);
SELECT pgraft_add_node(3, '127.0.0.1', 7003);

-- Get cluster status
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_cluster_status();
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'Core Functions',
              content: `**Basic Operations:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Initialize a new node
SELECT pgraft_init();

-- Check if current node is leader
SELECT pgraft_is_leader();

-- Get cluster status
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_cluster_status();
\`\`\`

**Cluster Management:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Add a new node to the cluster (only on leader)
SELECT pgraft_add_node(2, '127.0.0.1', 7002);
SELECT pgraft_add_node(3, '127.0.0.1', 7003);

-- Get cluster membership
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_cluster_info();

-- Remove a node from the cluster
SELECT pgraft_remove_node('node2');
\`\`\`

**Monitoring Functions:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Get detailed cluster status
SELECT * FROM pgraft_cluster_status();

-- Get node health information
SELECT * FROM pgraft_node_health();

-- Get consensus metrics
SELECT * FROM pgraft_consensus_metrics();

-- Get log information
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_log_info();
\`\`\`

**Administrative Functions:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Force a leader election (use with caution)
SELECT pgraft_force_election();

-- Pause consensus (for maintenance)
SELECT pgraft_pause_consensus();

-- Resume consensus
SELECT pgraft_resume_consensus();

-- Get consensus log entries
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_log_entries(100, 200);
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'Configuration',
              content: `**Default Configuration:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Consensus parameters (defaults)
pgraft.heartbeat_interval = '100ms'        -- Heartbeat interval
pgraft.election_timeout = '1000ms'         -- Election timeout
pgraft.max_log_entries = 10000            -- Max log entries before snapshot

-- Network settings
pgraft.listen_addr = '0.0.0.0:7001'       -- Address to listen on
pgraft.data_dir = '/var/lib/pgraft'       -- Data directory for consensus state
\`\`\`

**Cluster Setup:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Set cluster configuration (if needed)
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.cluster_id = 'postgres-cluster';
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.node_id = 'node1';
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.listen_addr = '0.0.0.0:7001';

-- Reload configuration
SELECT pg_reload_conf();
\`\`\`

**Performance Tuning:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Adjust consensus parameters for your environment
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.heartbeat_interval = '50ms';   -- Faster heartbeats
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.election_timeout = '500ms';    -- Faster elections
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.max_log_entries = 5000;       -- Smaller log size

-- Reload configuration
SELECT pg_reload_conf();
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'Usage Examples',
              content: `**Setting up a 3-node cluster:**
\`\`\`sql
-- On node1 (initial setup)
CREATE EXTENSION pgraft;
SELECT pgraft_init();

-- Check if leader
SELECT pgraft_is_leader();

-- On node2
CREATE EXTENSION pgraft;
SELECT pgraft_init();

-- On node3
CREATE EXTENSION pgraft;
SELECT pgraft_init();

-- Add nodes to cluster (from leader)
SELECT pgraft_add_node(2, '127.0.0.1', 7002);
SELECT pgraft_add_node(3, '127.0.0.1', 7003);

-- Get cluster status
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_cluster_status();
\`\`\`

**Monitoring cluster health:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Check cluster status
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_cluster_status();

-- Check node health
SELECT * FROM pgraft_node_health();

-- Get consensus metrics
SELECT * FROM pgraft_consensus_metrics();

-- Monitor leader changes
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION monitor_leader_changes()
RETURNS void AS $$
DECLARE
    current_leader text;
    previous_leader text := '';
BEGIN
    LOOP
        SELECT pgraft_is_leader() INTO current_leader;
        
        IF current_leader != previous_leader THEN
            RAISE NOTICE 'Leader changed: %', current_leader;
            previous_leader := current_leader;
        END IF;
        
        PERFORM pg_sleep(1);
    END LOOP;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
\`\`\`

**Production Deployment:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Production-ready cluster setup
CREATE EXTENSION pgraft;

-- Initialize with production settings
SELECT pgraft_init();

-- Configure for production
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.heartbeat_interval = '50ms';
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.election_timeout = '500ms';
SELECT pg_reload_conf();

-- Add production nodes
SELECT pgraft_add_node(2, 'prod-node2', 7002);
SELECT pgraft_add_node(3, 'prod-node3', 7003);

-- Verify cluster health
SELECT * FROM pgraft_cluster_status();
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'Troubleshooting and Diagnostics',
              content: `**Common Issues and Solutions:**

**1. Node not joining cluster:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Check if node is initialized
SELECT pgraft_is_leader();

-- Check cluster status
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_cluster_status();

-- Verify node is added correctly
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_cluster_info();
\`\`\`

**2. Cluster not forming:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Check if all nodes are initialized
SELECT pgraft_init();

-- Verify network connectivity
-- Ensure all nodes can reach each other on configured ports

-- Check consensus metrics
SELECT * FROM pgraft_consensus_metrics();
\`\`\`

**3. Leader election issues:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Check current leader
SELECT pgraft_is_leader();

-- Force election if needed (use with caution)
SELECT pgraft_force_election();

-- Monitor consensus metrics
SELECT * FROM pgraft_consensus_metrics();
\`\`\`

**Diagnostic Queries:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Get comprehensive cluster status
SELECT 
    c.node_id,
    c.state,
    c.is_leader,
    h.last_heartbeat,
    h.connection_count,
    r.replication_lag,
    m.election_count,
    m.heartbeat_count
FROM pgraft_cluster_status() c
LEFT JOIN pgraft_node_health() h ON c.node_id = h.node_id
LEFT JOIN pgraft_replication_lag() r ON c.node_id = r.node_id
LEFT JOIN pgraft_consensus_metrics() m ON c.node_id = m.node_id;

-- Check for split-brain conditions
SELECT 
    node_id,
    state,
    last_heartbeat,
    CASE 
        WHEN last_heartbeat < NOW() - INTERVAL '5 seconds' THEN 'STALE'
        ELSE 'ACTIVE'
    END as heartbeat_status
FROM pgraft_node_health();
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'Architecture Deep Dive',
              content: `**pgraft Architecture:**
pgraft implements the Raft consensus algorithm as a PostgreSQL extension, providing distributed consensus with strong consistency guarantees.

**Core Components:**
1. **PostgreSQL Background Worker (C)**: Drives Raft ticks every 100ms
2. **pgraft_go_tick() [C→Go]**: Bridge between C and Go components
3. **raftNode.Tick() [etcd-io/raft]**: Core Raft implementation
4. **raftProcessingLoop() [Goroutine]**: Handles Ready() messages
5. **Persist → Send → Apply → Advance**: Raft state machine flow

**Data Flow:**
\`\`\`
PostgreSQL Background Worker (C)
    ↓ Every 100ms
pgraft_go_tick() [C→Go]
    ↓
raftNode.Tick() [etcd-io/raft]
    ↓
Ready() messages
    ↓
raftProcessingLoop() [Goroutine]
    ↓
Persist → Send → Apply → Advance
\`\`\`

**Key Design Decisions:**
- **Worker-Driven**: PostgreSQL background worker actively drives Raft ticks
- **Persistent Storage**: HardState, log entries, and snapshots survive crashes
- **Zero Configuration**: Minimal setup required for basic operation
- **Production Ready**: 0 compilation errors/warnings, PostgreSQL C coding standards compliant`
            },
            {
              title: 'Split-Brain Protection',
              content: `**100% Split-Brain Protection:**
pgraft provides mathematical guarantees against split-brain scenarios through the Raft consensus algorithm.

**Protection Mechanisms:**
1. **Quorum Requirement**: Leader needs majority votes (N/2 + 1)
2. **Term Monotonicity**: Higher term always wins elections
3. **Log Completeness**: Only up-to-date nodes can be elected leader
4. **Single Leader Per Term**: Mathematical guarantee from Raft algorithm

**Example Scenario:**
\`\`\`sql
-- 3-node cluster with network partition
-- Node 1 and 2 can communicate, Node 3 is isolated

-- Node 1 (Leader): Can maintain leadership with 2/3 votes
SELECT pgraft_is_leader(); -- Returns true

-- Node 3 (Isolated): Cannot become leader (only 1/3 votes)
SELECT pgraft_is_leader(); -- Returns false

-- When network heals, Node 3 catches up automatically
SELECT * FROM pgraft_get_cluster_status();
\`\`\`

**Automatic Recovery:**
- Isolated nodes automatically rejoin when connectivity is restored
- Log replication ensures consistency across all nodes
- No manual intervention required for split-brain recovery`
            },
            {
              title: 'Performance Optimization',
              content: `**Performance Characteristics:**
- **Tick Interval**: 100ms (worker-driven)
- **Election Timeout**: 1000ms (default, configurable)
- **Heartbeat**: 100ms (default, configurable)
- **Memory**: ~50MB per node
- **CPU**: <1% idle, <5% during elections

**Optimization Strategies:**
\`\`\`sql
-- For high-performance environments
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.heartbeat_interval = '50ms';   -- Faster heartbeats
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.election_timeout = '500ms';    -- Faster elections
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.max_log_entries = 5000;       -- Smaller log size

-- For stability in unstable networks
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.heartbeat_interval = '200ms';  -- Slower heartbeats
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.election_timeout = '2000ms';   -- Longer elections
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.max_log_entries = 20000;      -- Larger log size

SELECT pg_reload_conf();
\`\`\`

**Monitoring Performance:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Check consensus metrics
SELECT * FROM pgraft_consensus_metrics();

-- Monitor node health
SELECT * FROM pgraft_node_health();

-- Get cluster performance stats
SELECT 
    node_id,
    is_leader,
    heartbeat_count,
    election_count,
    log_size
FROM pgraft_cluster_status();
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'Production Deployment',
              content: `**Production Checklist:**

**Prerequisites:**
- PostgreSQL 17+ (recommended)
- Go 1.21+ (for building from source)
- Stable network connectivity between nodes
- Sufficient disk space for logs and snapshots

**Deployment Steps:**
\`\`\`sql
-- 1. Install extension on all nodes
CREATE EXTENSION pgraft;

-- 2. Initialize nodes
SELECT pgraft_init();

-- 3. Configure cluster (on leader)
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.cluster_id = 'production-cluster';
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.node_id = 'prod-node1';
SELECT pg_reload_conf();

-- 4. Add nodes to cluster (from leader)
SELECT pgraft_add_node(2, 'prod-node2', 7002);
SELECT pgraft_add_node(3, 'prod-node3', 7003);

-- 5. Verify cluster health
SELECT * FROM pgraft_cluster_status();
\`\`\`

**Monitoring Setup:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Create monitoring view
CREATE VIEW pgraft_production_monitoring AS
SELECT 
    node_id,
    is_leader,
    last_heartbeat,
    CASE 
        WHEN last_heartbeat < NOW() - INTERVAL '5 seconds' THEN 'WARNING'
        WHEN last_heartbeat < NOW() - INTERVAL '10 seconds' THEN 'CRITICAL'
        ELSE 'OK'
    END as health_status
FROM pgraft_cluster_status();

-- Schedule monitoring query
SELECT * FROM pgraft_production_monitoring;
\`\`\`

**Backup Strategy:**
- pgraft state is automatically persisted
- Regular PostgreSQL backups include consensus state
- Snapshots are taken automatically when log size exceeds threshold`
            },
            {
              title: 'Best Practices',
              content: `**Cluster Design:**
- Use odd number of nodes (3, 5, 7) for optimal quorum
- Ensure stable network connectivity between all nodes
- Place nodes in different availability zones for fault tolerance

**Configuration:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Recommended production settings
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.heartbeat_interval = '100ms';
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.election_timeout = '1000ms';
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.max_log_entries = 10000;

-- For high-availability setups
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.heartbeat_interval = '50ms';
ALTER SYSTEM SET pgraft.election_timeout = '500ms';
\`\`\`

**Operational Guidelines:**
1. **Node Addition**: Always add nodes from the current leader
2. **Maintenance**: Use pgraft_pause_consensus() for planned maintenance
3. **Monitoring**: Set up alerts for heartbeat failures
4. **Logs**: Monitor log size and snapshot frequency

**Common Patterns:**
\`\`\`sql
-- Check cluster before maintenance
SELECT * FROM pgraft_cluster_status();

-- Pause consensus for maintenance
SELECT pgraft_pause_consensus();

-- Perform maintenance operations
-- ...

-- Resume consensus
SELECT pgraft_resume_consensus();

-- Verify cluster health
SELECT * FROM pgraft_node_health();
\`\`\``
