        'ramd Documentation': {
          sections: [
            {
              title: 'Cluster Daemon Overview',
              content: `ramd is the cluster management daemon that monitors PostgreSQL instances and coordinates failover operations in RAM clusters.

**Key Responsibilities:**
- Monitor PostgreSQL instance health and availability
- Coordinate failover operations when primary fails
- Provide REST API for cluster management
- Expose Prometheus metrics for monitoring
- Manage cluster membership and node status
- Handle automatic recovery and rebalancing

**Architecture:**
ramd runs as a system daemon on each cluster node and communicates with:
- Local PostgreSQL instance via pgraft extension
- Other ramd instances for cluster coordination
- External monitoring systems via REST API and metrics
- Load balancers and application clients for health checks`
            },
            {
              title: 'Configuration',
              content: `**Main Configuration File:** \`/etc/ram/ramd.conf\`

\`\`\`toml
# Cluster configuration
[cluster]
name = "postgres-cluster"
node_id = "node1"
data_dir = "/var/lib/ram"
log_level = "info"

# PostgreSQL connection settings
[postgresql]
host = "localhost"
port = 5432
database = "postgres"
user = "postgres"
password = "secure_password"
ssl_mode = "prefer"

# Raft consensus settings
[raft]
listen_addr = "0.0.0.0:8080"
heartbeat_interval = "100ms"
election_timeout = "1000ms"
max_log_entries = 10000
snapshot_threshold = 1000

# Monitoring and metrics
[monitoring]
prometheus_port = 9090
health_check_interval = "5s"
metrics_retention = "24h"

# API settings
[api]
listen_addr = "0.0.0.0:8081"
enable_tls = false
tls_cert_file = "/etc/ssl/certs/ramd.crt"
tls_key_file = "/etc/ssl/private/ramd.key"

# Logging configuration
[logging]
log_file = "/var/log/ram/ramd.log"
max_file_size = "100MB"
max_files = 5
\`\`\`

**Environment Variables:**
\`\`\`bash
export RAM_CLUSTER_NAME="postgres-cluster"
export RAM_NODE_ID="node1"
export RAM_DATA_DIR="/var/lib/ram"
export RAM_LOG_LEVEL="info"
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'HTTP API Reference',
              content: `ramd provides a comprehensive REST API for cluster management and monitoring.

**Authentication:**
All API endpoints support token-based authentication:
\`\`\`bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" http://localhost:8081/api/v1/status
\`\`\`

**Cluster Management Endpoints:**
\`\`\`bash
# Get cluster status
GET /api/v1/cluster/status
Response: {
  "cluster_name": "postgres-cluster",
  "leader": "node1",
  "nodes": [
    {"id": "node1", "role": "leader", "status": "healthy"},
    {"id": "node2", "role": "follower", "status": "healthy"},
    {"id": "node3", "role": "follower", "status": "healthy"}
  ],
  "health": "healthy"
}

# List all nodes
GET /api/v1/cluster/nodes
Response: [
  {
    "id": "node1",
    "address": "192.168.1.101:5432",
    "role": "leader",
    "status": "healthy",
    "last_heartbeat": "2024-01-27T10:30:00Z"
  }
]

# Trigger manual failover
POST /api/v1/cluster/failover
Body: {"target_node": "node2", "force": false}

# Add node to cluster
POST /api/v1/cluster/nodes
Body: {"id": "node4", "address": "192.168.1.104:5432"}

# Remove node from cluster
DELETE /api/v1/cluster/nodes/{node_id}
\`\`\`

**Monitoring Endpoints:**
\`\`\`bash
# Get Prometheus metrics
GET /api/v1/metrics
Response: Prometheus format metrics

# Get cluster health
GET /api/v1/health
Response: {
  "status": "healthy",
  "checks": {
    "postgresql": "ok",
    "raft": "ok",
    "disk_space": "ok"
  }
}

# Get node health
GET /api/v1/nodes/{node_id}/health
Response: {
  "node_id": "node1",
  "status": "healthy",
  "postgresql_uptime": "7d 12h 30m",
  "replication_lag": "0ms",
  "disk_usage": "45%"
}
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'Operational Commands',
              content: `**Starting ramd:**
\`\`\`bash
# Start as daemon
ramd --config /etc/ram/ramd.conf --daemon

# Start in foreground (for debugging)
ramd --config /etc/ram/ramd.conf --foreground

# Start with custom log level
ramd --config /etc/ram/ramd.conf --log-level debug
\`\`\`

**Stopping ramd:**
\`\`\`bash
# Graceful shutdown
ramd --stop

# Force stop
ramd --stop --force

# Send SIGTERM to running daemon
kill -TERM $(pidof ramd)
\`\`\`

**Status and Health Checks:**
\`\`\`bash
# Check daemon status
ramd --status

# Test configuration
ramd --config /etc/ram/ramd.conf --test-config

# Show version and build info
ramd --version
\`\`\`

**Log Management:**
\`\`\`bash
# View logs in real-time
tail -f /var/log/ram/ramd.log

# Rotate logs
ramd --rotate-logs

# Check log file sizes
ls -lh /var/log/ram/
\`\`\``
            },
            {
              title: 'Monitoring and Metrics',
              content: `**Prometheus Metrics:**
ramd exposes comprehensive metrics for monitoring cluster health and performance.

**Key Metrics:**
\`\`\`
# Cluster metrics
ram_cluster_nodes_total{cluster="postgres-cluster"} 3
ram_cluster_leader_changes_total{cluster="postgres-cluster"} 2
ram_cluster_health_status{cluster="postgres-cluster",status="healthy"} 1

# Node metrics
ram_node_status{cluster="postgres-cluster",node="node1",status="leader"} 1
ram_node_uptime_seconds{cluster="postgres-cluster",node="node1"} 604800
ram_node_replication_lag_ms{cluster="postgres-cluster",node="node2"} 5

# PostgreSQL metrics
ram_postgresql_connections{cluster="postgres-cluster",node="node1"} 25
ram_postgresql_queries_per_second{cluster="postgres-cluster",node="node1"} 150
ram_postgresql_wal_lag_bytes{cluster="postgres-cluster",node="node2"} 1024

# Raft metrics
ram_raft_term{cluster="postgres-cluster",node="node1"} 5
ram_raft_committed_index{cluster="postgres-cluster",node="node1"} 10000
ram_raft_applied_index{cluster="postgres-cluster",node="node1"} 9995
\`\`\`

**Health Check Endpoints:**
\`\`\`bash
# Basic health check
curl http://localhost:8081/api/v1/health

# Detailed health check
curl http://localhost:8081/api/v1/health/detailed

# Node-specific health
curl http://localhost:8081/api/v1/nodes/node1/health
\`\`\`

**Alerting Rules (Prometheus):**
\`\`\`yaml
groups:
- name: ram_cluster
  rules:
  - alert: ClusterDown
    expr: ram_cluster_health_status == 0
    for: 1m
    labels:
      severity: critical
    annotations:
      summary: "RAM cluster is down"
      
  - alert: NodeDown
    expr: ram_node_status == 0
    for: 30s
    labels:
      severity: warning
    annotations:
      summary: "RAM node {{ $labels.node }} is down"
      
  - alert: HighReplicationLag
    expr: ram_node_replication_lag_ms > 1000
    for: 2m
    labels:
      severity: warning
    annotations:
      summary: "High replication lag on node {{ $labels.node }}"
\`\`\``
